# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase configuration for United Jewel Pack
#
# 1. Copy this file to  .env.local  (for `npm run dev`)  and/or  .env.production.local
#    (for `npm run build`).  Those files are git-ignored — never commit real values.
# 2. Replace the placeholders with the values from
#       Firebase console → Project settings → General → Your apps → Web app → SDK setup
#
# These are the Firebase *web app* identifiers. They are NOT secrets (every visitor's
# browser receives them); your data is protected by Authentication + Firestore Security
# Rules, not by hiding these. They are still kept out of git and injected at build time.
#
# Leave them all blank (or delete the file) and the app runs exactly as before, storing
# everything in the browser — handy for trying things out without Firebase.
#
# Never put a service-account key, an Admin SDK key or any private key in this project.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=unitedjewelpack.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=unitedjewelpack
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
